IMPORT prelude

-- Commodity Trading Act 1992 (Singapore) -- who must hold a licence (ss 12, 13, 13A, 14A and the Schedule, with the 8 October 2018
-- cessation in ss 12(2) and 13(2)), the meaning of "accredited investor" (Schedule para 2), approval of commodity markets and clearing
-- houses (ss 4, 8), risk disclosure before dealing (s 32), and the penalties and prosecution rules (ss 12(3), 13(4), 13A(3), 33, 49,
-- 57, 58, 60).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/CTA1992.txt, with amendments to
-- Act 25 of 2021 (in force 1 April 2022) shown.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Cited by 8 of the 527 Singapore Acts deposited in this repository. SCOPED to the licensing gate and the conduct and
-- market-abuse offences a broker, adviser, pool operator or trader actually meets. Not encoded: the Board's approval criteria and
-- business rules (ss 5, 6, 9), revocation of approvals (s 7), liability of markets (s 11), grounds for refusing or revoking a
-- licence (ss 15, 18, 19), accounts and audit (Part 4), segregation of funds (ss 30, 31), the Board's powers (Part 6), secrecy and
-- the remaining Part 8 offences, and Schedule item 1(a) (ordinary-course purchases and sales off a commodity market). The
-- "transitional licence" of s 13(2) is defined by "section 66", which is NOT in the deposited text; it is taken here as a bare fact.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Commodity Trading Act 1992 -- licensing`

DECLARE Role IS ONE OF
    `a commodity broker`
    `a commodity broker's representative`
    `a commodity trading adviser`
    `a commodity trading adviser's representative`
    `a commodity pool operator`
    `a commodity pool operator's representative`
    `a spot commodity broker`
    `a spot commodity broker's representative`
    `a spot commodity pool operator`
    `a spot commodity pool operator's representative`

-- For a representative, `started on or after 8 October 2018` describes the business of the broker, adviser or pool operator the
-- representative acts for (s 13(2)(a), (c), (e) look to the principal "mentioned in section 12(2)" or in para (b) or (d)).
DECLARE Person HAS
    `role` IS A Role
    `started on or after 8 October 2018` IS A BOOLEAN
    `holds a transitional licence` IS A BOOLEAN
    `holds a licence authorising the role` IS A BOOLEAN
    `deals only with accredited investors` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is a licensed bank or merchant bank` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is a Finance and Treasury Centre or approved oil or international commodity trading company` IS A BOOLEAN
    `trades spot only on own account and solicits no public funds` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is not a party, carries no customer position and takes no customer money` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the commodity is physically delivered` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the role` IS A Role
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a spot role` IF
    CONSIDER `the role`
    WHEN `a spot commodity broker` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a spot commodity broker's representative` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a spot commodity pool operator` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a spot commodity pool operator's representative` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `12(2), 13(2) -- the 8 October 2018 cessation`

-- s 12(2): "As from 8 October 2018, subsection (1) ceases to apply to any person who commences business as a commodity broker on or
-- after that date." s 13(2): the same for a trading adviser (b) and pool operator (d) who commence on or after that date, and for a
-- representative of such a broker, adviser or pool operator "who does not hold a transitional licence" (a), (c), (e).
-- s 13A (spot commodity trading) has NO such subsection.
GIVEN `the person` IS A Person
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the 2018 cessation applies` IF
    CONSIDER `the person`'s `role`
    WHEN `a commodity broker` THEN `the person`'s `started on or after 8 October 2018`
    WHEN `a commodity trading adviser` THEN `the person`'s `started on or after 8 October 2018`
    WHEN `a commodity pool operator` THEN `the person`'s `started on or after 8 October 2018`
    WHEN `a commodity broker's representative` THEN
        `the person`'s `started on or after 8 October 2018` AND (NOT `the person`'s `holds a transitional licence`)
    WHEN `a commodity trading adviser's representative` THEN
        `the person`'s `started on or after 8 October 2018` AND (NOT `the person`'s `holds a transitional licence`)
    WHEN `a commodity pool operator's representative` THEN
        `the person`'s `started on or after 8 October 2018` AND (NOT `the person`'s `holds a transitional licence`)
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `14A and the Schedule -- exemptions`

-- Schedule item 1: (b) for s 12(1), a person soliciting or accepting orders who "is not a party", "does not carry the customer's
-- position, margin or account", "does not accept money or assets", and "there is physical delivery"; (c) for ss 12(1) and 13(1),
-- a person trading "only with accredited investors"; (d) for ss 12(1) and 13(1), a licensed bank or merchant bank; (e) for
-- ss 12(1) and 13(1), a Finance and Treasury Centre, approved oil trading company or approved international commodity trading
-- company; (f) for s 13A, a person trading spot "on the person's own account" who "does not solicit any funds from any member of
-- the public"; (g) for s 13A, the order-taker of (b) WITHOUT the physical-delivery condition.
-- Items (c), (d) and (e) do not extend to s 13A. Item (b) is in respect of s 12(1) only, not s 13(1).
GIVEN `the person` IS A Person
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a Schedule exemption applies` IF
    IF `is a spot role` (`the person`'s `role`)
    THEN     `the person`'s `trades spot only on own account and solicits no public funds`
         OR  `the person`'s `is not a party, carries no customer position and takes no customer money`
    ELSE     `the person`'s `deals only with accredited investors`
         OR  `the person`'s `is a licensed bank or merchant bank`
         OR  `the person`'s `is a Finance and Treasury Centre or approved oil or international commodity trading company`
         OR  `the order-taker exemption for brokers applies` `the person`

GIVEN `the person` IS A Person
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the order-taker exemption for brokers applies` IF
    CONSIDER `the person`'s `role`
    WHEN `a commodity broker` THEN
            `the person`'s `is not a party, carries no customer position and takes no customer money`
        AND `the person`'s `the commodity is physically delivered`
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `12(1), 13(1), 13A(1) -- the licence requirement`

-- s 12(1): no person may carry on business as a commodity broker "unless the person (i) is licensed ... and (ii) trades in
-- accordance with the business rules and practices of a commodity market". s 13(1), 13A(1): no person may act as a representative,
-- trading adviser, pool operator, spot broker or spot pool operator "unless the person is the holder of a licence granted under this
-- Part that authorises the person to act as such". (Limb (ii) of s 12(1) is not modelled.)
GIVEN `the person` IS A Person
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a licence is required` IF
        (NOT `the 2018 cessation applies` `the person`)
    AND (NOT `a Schedule exemption applies` `the person`)

GIVEN `the person` IS A Person
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `acting is an unlicensed-activity offence` IF
        `a licence is required` `the person`
    AND (NOT `the person`'s `holds a licence authorising the role`)

-- s 12(3): $100,000 or 3 years. s 13(4)(a): adviser and pool operator $100,000 or 3 years; (b): their representatives and broker's
-- representatives $50,000 or 12 months. s 13A(3): spot broker and spot pool operator $100,000 or 3 years; their representatives
-- $50,000 or 12 months. "or to both" in every case.
GIVEN `the role` IS A Role
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine for unlicensed activity` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the role`
    WHEN `a commodity broker's representative` THEN 50000
    WHEN `a commodity trading adviser's representative` THEN 50000
    WHEN `a commodity pool operator's representative` THEN 50000
    WHEN `a spot commodity broker's representative` THEN 50000
    WHEN `a spot commodity pool operator's representative` THEN 50000
    OTHERWISE 100000

GIVEN `the role` IS A Role
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum imprisonment in months for unlicensed activity` MEANS
    IF `the maximum fine for unlicensed activity` `the role` EQUALS 50000 THEN 12 ELSE 36

§§ `Schedule para 2 -- accredited investor`

-- "(a) an individual -- (i) whose net personal assets EXCEED $2 million ... or (ii) whose income in the preceding 12 months is NOT
-- LESS THAN $300,000"; "(b) a corporation with net assets EXCEEDING $10 million" (by its latest audited, or certified, balance
-- sheet). The Board may prescribe other amounts; trustees and other prescribed persons ((c), (d)) are not modelled.
GIVEN `is a corporation` IS A BOOLEAN, `net assets` IS A NUMBER, `income in the preceding 12 months` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is an accredited investor` IF
    IF `is a corporation`
    THEN `net assets` GREATER THAN 10000000
    ELSE `net assets` GREATER THAN 2000000 OR `income in the preceding 12 months` AT LEAST 300000

§§ `4, 8 -- approval of commodity markets and clearing houses`

-- s 4(1): no person may establish or maintain a commodity market "unless the commodity market has been approved by the Board".
-- (2): "As from 8 October 2018, subsection (1) ceases to apply in relation to any commodity market -- (a) that is established on or
-- after that date; or (b) that was approved ... before that date, to the extent that it relates to commodity forward contracts."
-- s 8(1), (2): the same for a clearing house. (3) in each: $30,000 or 3 years or both.
GIVEN `established on or after 8 October 2018` IS A BOOLEAN, `approved before that date` IS A BOOLEAN, `relates to forward contracts` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `approval of the market is required` IF
        (NOT `established on or after 8 October 2018`)
    AND (NOT (`approved before that date` AND `relates to forward contracts`))

§§ `32 -- risk disclosure`

-- s 32(1): no commodity broker may open a commodity contract account "unless the commodity broker furnishes the customer with a
-- separate written risk disclosure document ... and receives from the customer an acknowledgment signed and dated by the customer".
GIVEN `a separate written disclosure document was furnished` IS A BOOLEAN, `the acknowledgment is signed` IS A BOOLEAN, `the acknowledgment is dated` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the broker may open the account` IF
        `a separate written disclosure document was furnished`
    AND `the acknowledgment is signed`
    AND `the acknowledgment is dated`

-- s 32(2): a pool operator may not solicit, accept or receive funds from a prospective participant "unless, ON OR BEFORE THE DATE it
-- engages in that activity", it delivers the document and receives a signed and dated acknowledgment. Days are counted as numbers.
GIVEN `day the document is delivered` IS A NUMBER, `day funds are solicited` IS A NUMBER, `signed and dated acknowledgment received` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the pool operator may solicit funds` IF
        `day the document is delivered` AT MOST `day funds are solicited`
    AND `signed and dated acknowledgment received`

-- s 32(3): a trading adviser may not solicit or enter into a managing agreement unless "at or before the time [it] engages in the
-- solicitation or enters into the agreement (WHICHEVER IS THE EARLIER)" it delivers the document and receives the acknowledgment.
GIVEN `a` IS A NUMBER, `b` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the earlier of` MEANS IF `a` AT MOST `b` THEN `a` ELSE `b`

GIVEN `day the adviser's document is delivered` IS A NUMBER, `day of solicitation` IS A NUMBER, `day of the agreement` IS A NUMBER, `adviser received the acknowledgment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the adviser complies with section 32(3)` IF
        `day the adviser's document is delivered` AT MOST `the earlier of` `day of solicitation` `day of the agreement`
    AND `adviser received the acknowledgment`

§§ `33, 49, 57, 60 -- penalties`

-- s 33 (Part 5, which includes s 32): "$30,000 or ... 3 years or ... both". s 49 (Part 7 -- false trading, bucketing, spreading
-- false-trading information, manipulation and cornering, fraudulent devices, fraudulently inducing trading, ss 43-48): "(a) in the
-- case of an individual, ... $250,000 or ... 7 years or ... both; or (b) in the case of a body corporate, ... $500,000".
DECLARE Offender IS ONE OF
    `an individual`
    `a body corporate`

GIVEN `the offender` IS AN Offender
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the Part 7 maximum fine` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offender`
    WHEN `an individual` THEN 250000
    WHEN `a body corporate` THEN 500000

GIVEN `the offender` IS AN Offender
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the Part 7 maximum imprisonment in years` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offender`
    WHEN `an individual` THEN 7
    WHEN `a body corporate` THEN 0

-- s 57(3) (misuse of the titles "clearing house", "commodity broker", "commodity trading adviser", "commodity pool operator" and
-- the spot titles): "$20,000 and, in the case of a continuing offence, to a further fine of $2,000 for every day during which the
-- offence continues after conviction".
GIVEN `days continued after conviction` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine for misusing a title` MEANS 20000 PLUS 2000 TIMES `days continued after conviction`

-- s 60: no penalty expressly provided -- "a fine not exceeding $20,000".
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the general penalty` MEANS 20000

§§ `58 -- who prosecutes, and composition`

-- s 58(1): proceedings "(a) against any provision in Part 7 may be taken ONLY with the consent of the Public Prosecutor; and (b)
-- against any other provision ... may be taken by the Board or, with the consent of the Public Prosecutor, by any other person".
GIVEN `is a Part 7 offence` IS A BOOLEAN, `the prosecutor is the Board` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Public Prosecutor's consent is needed` IF
        `is a Part 7 offence`
    OR  (NOT `the prosecutor is the Board`)

-- s 58(2), (3): for an offence "punishable only by a fine", the Board may demand the fine or a reduced amount; "if the person pays
-- that amount to the Board within 14 days after the demand, no proceedings may be taken". Only "where a person admits the offence
-- and agrees in writing".
GIVEN `punishable only by a fine` IS A BOOLEAN, `admits the offence` IS A BOOLEAN, `agrees in writing` IS A BOOLEAN, `days after the demand when paid` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `composition bars proceedings` IF
        `punishable only by a fine`
    AND `admits the offence`
    AND `agrees in writing`
    AND `days after the demand when paid` AT MOST 14
